From 07f9910424a80e78e77c863cbc5ffd5065a30262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 10:47:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0231 -- v1.0.9 HQ tier: true 22050 stereo Organya
 pre-render

DOS port. The opt-in HQ audio tier (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_TIER2=0 ->
22050 Hz / 2ch) was only half-wired: the Organya pre-render path
downmixed the synth's interleaved L/R to mono and the playback producer
dual-mono-duplicated it onto the stereo device, so a Tier-1 device got
dual-mono, not the org's true panning -- and the precache batch refused
a stereo tier outright (it would write mono content tagged channels=2).
The 11025-mono LQ tier is the 486 production default, but faster DOS
hardware can afford the original Cave Story 2004 fidelity, which also
resolves the known 11025 "scratch".

Closes the stereo gaps end-to-end:
- _org_render_song gains a channels arg; channels==2 pushes interleaved
  L,R (per-channel box-decim, no average) so the synth panning survives
  into the cache. Mono path byte-identical. Loop wrap target kept
  frame-aligned (even) for stereo.
- the pre-render producer reads interleaved L,R from a stereo buffer
  instead of duplicating L; mono-buffer dual-mono path retained as the
  fallback. startBeat seek accounts for channels.
- both stereo-refusal guards (SoundManager::precacheAllOrgs + main.cpp
  first-launch auto-precache) removed -- both tiers now render to the
  tier-keyed cache (CACHE\22050_2\ for HQ).
- cache header loopstart_frame documented as a buffer int16 index.

Opt-in, default OFF (production stays Tier-2 LQ); real fps cost on
486-class HW (4x SB16 output bandwidth). Distinct one-shot init banner
[org-hq] for the smoke gate. See docs/internal/V109-AUDIO-MATRIX-DESIGN.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
